IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g1-art1-defined-terms`
IMPORT `g1-art2-entity`

-- g1-art2-governor-misconduct.l4: Article 2(7) to (10) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: "governor", "relevant unincorporated entity", the two clarifications of (9), and "misconduct".
-- Source: the consolidated text "from 2 October 2026", INPUTS/charities-jersey-law-2014-2026-10-02.txt; every quotation is a slice of that file (src:N is line N).
--
-- How the module is built.
--   * "Governor" is a list of cases, like the definitions above it: a trustee or fidéicommissaire, a council member, a director, a member of a management committee, and in any other case a
--     person with the general control and management. Which cases apply depends on the kinds of entity (Article 2(1)), so the rules take the entity's list of kinds. A person's role is a
--     fact about the person (the record `Facts about a person's role in an entity`); who a trustee, a director or a council member is, is an input (the other enactments are out of scope).
--   * A body in more than one kind (a company that is the sole trustee) is in more than one case: fork F1.4. The paragraph (e) "in any other case" is read as the residue: it applies when none of (a) to (d) does.
--   * "Misconduct" is a contravention by a registered charity or its governors (a), or an offence in relation to a charity (b). Whether a provision of this Law has been contravened is not decided here:
--     every duty and prohibition of the Law decides its own breach, and the caller passes the fact in (the standard input IP13). The same is true of the constitutional Law of the charity
--     (Article 2(5): the caller passes the list), of the required steps notices served (IP19) and of whether the entity is an excepted foreign charity (IP26).
--   * Forks of the group that live here: F1.2 (which limbs of (b) need the offence to be in relation to a charity), F1.4 (governors), F1.5 (through "published" in (8)(b)(i)), F1.7 (when the
--     standing of the charity is read). Each public decision that depends on one takes `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`.

§ `Part 1 — Interpretation`

§§ `2 Definition of entity and related terms`

§§§ `2(7) governor`

-- src:91 | (7) In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires, “governor” in relation to an entity means –
-- src:92 | (a) in the case of a trust or fidéicommis, a trustee or fidéicommissaire of the trust or fidéicommis;
-- src:93 | (b) in the case of a foundation, a member of the council of the foundation;
-- src:94 | (c) in the case of a company, a director of the company;
-- src:95 | (d) in the case of a relevant unincorporated entity, a person who is a member of the management committee of the entity; or
-- src:96 | (e) in any other case, a person who, under the constitution of the entity, has the general control and management of the administration of the entity.
-- The lead-in is "unless the context otherwise requires"; no place was found where the context displaces the list.

-- How a person stands to the general control and management of the administration of an entity under its constitution. The three ways of having it, or not, that paragraph (9) speaks of.
DECLARE `Relation to the general control and management` IS ONE OF
    `holds the general control and management alone`
    `holds the general control and management as one of a number of governors`
    `exercises the general control and management only on behalf of another who holds it in that other's own right`
    `holds none of the general control and management`

DECLARE `Facts about a person's role in an entity` HAS
    `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(7)(a): the person is a trustee of the trust, or a fidéicommissaire of the court-approved fidéicommis
    `a member of the council of the foundation` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(7)(b): the person is a member of the council of the foundation
    `a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(7)(c): the person is a director of the company
    `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(7)(d): the person is a member of the management committee of the entity
    `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS A `Relation to the general control and management`
        @desc Article 2(7)(e) and 2(9): whether, under the constitution, the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity alone, as one of a number, only exercises it for another who has it in that other's own right, or has none of it

§§§ `2(8) relevant unincorporated entity`

-- src:97 | (8) For the purpose of paragraph (7)(d) a relevant unincorporated entity is an unincorporated body or association of persons that –
-- src:98 | (a) falls within paragraph (1)(i); and
-- src:99 | (b) has a constitution that conforms to a model that –
-- src:100 | (i) is published for the purpose by the Commissioner, and
-- src:101 | (ii) provides for the entity to have a management committee.
-- "Conforms to a model" is a judgement and an input. "Published" is the Article 1 definition (the publisher's opinion, fork F1.5): a model the Commissioner honestly thinks adequately
-- published, but which is posted where nobody would see it, is published on reading A and not on reading B.
DECLARE `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` HAS
    `the constitution conforms to the model` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(8)(b): the entity's constitution conforms to the model
    `published by the Commissioner` IS A `Facts about a publication`
        @desc Article 2(8)(b)(i): what the Commissioner did to publish the model, what the Commissioner thought of the manner, and whether the manner is in fact likely to reach the audience
    `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(8)(b)(i): the model was published for the purpose of defining a relevant unincorporated entity
    `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(8)(b)(ii): the model provides for the entity to have a management committee

@ref Article 2(8)(a) (src:98)
GIVEN kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(8)(a) the entity falls within Article 2(1)(i)` kinds MEANS
    elem `an unincorporated body or association of persons` kinds

@ref Article 2(8)(b)(i) (src:100)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      model IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(8)(b)(i) the model is published for the purpose by the Commissioner` interp model MEANS
        model's `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)`
    AND `Art 1 the information has been published` interp (model's `published by the Commissioner`)

@ref Article 2(8)(b)(ii) (src:101)
GIVEN model IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(8)(b)(ii) the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` model MEANS
    model's `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee`

@ref Article 2(8)(b) (src:99)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      model IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(8)(b) the constitution conforms to a model published by the Commissioner that provides for a management committee` interp model MEANS
        model's `the constitution conforms to the model`
    AND "(i)" ... `Art 2(8)(b)(i) the model is published for the purpose by the Commissioner` interp model
    AND "(ii)" ... `Art 2(8)(b)(ii) the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` model

@ref Article 2(8) (src:97-101)
@export Whether an entity is a "relevant unincorporated entity" under Article 2(8) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: an unincorporated body or association of persons whose constitution conforms to a model that the Commissioner has published for the purpose and that provides for a management committee
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork; the field `meaning of published` decides whether the Commissioner's opinion or the manner's likelihood makes the model published
      kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity` @desc The sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls, as the entity's `kinds of entity`
      model IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` @desc Whether the constitution conforms to a model, how the Commissioner published the model, and whether the model provides for a management committee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(8) the entity is a relevant unincorporated entity` interp kinds model MEANS
        `Art 2(8)(a) the entity falls within Article 2(1)(i)` kinds
    AND `Art 2(8)(b) the constitution conforms to a model published by the Commissioner that provides for a management committee` interp model

§§§ `2(9) general control and management`

-- src:102 | (9) For the purpose of paragraph (7)(e) –
-- src:103 | (a) a person is not a governor merely by virtue of exercising general control and management on behalf of another person who has the general control and management in that other person’s own right under the constitution of the entity; and
-- src:104 | (b) a person is a governor whether that person has that general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors.
-- Both are clarifications of (7)(e), and both are rules over the relation: (b) is "has it alone or as one of a number"; (a) is the exclusion of the person who only exercises it for another.
@ref Article 2(9)(b) (src:104)
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` person MEANS
    CONSIDER person's `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution`
    WHEN `holds the general control and management alone` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `holds the general control and management as one of a number of governors` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `exercises the general control and management only on behalf of another who holds it in that other's own right` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `holds none of the general control and management` THEN FALSE

@ref Article 2(9)(a) (src:103)
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(9)(a) the person only exercises the general control and management on behalf of another who has it in own right` person MEANS
    person's `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution`
        EQUALS `exercises the general control and management only on behalf of another who holds it in that other's own right`

-- (e): "in any other case". The person who has the control under the constitution, alone or as one of a number (9)(b). Paragraph (9)(a) needs no clause of its own here: a person who only
-- exercises the control for another who has it in own right is not a person who "has" it, and the tests assert that (the clause is declaratory, as the phrasebook's "avoidance of doubt" entry says).
@ref Article 2(7)(e) (src:96)
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(7)(e) the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` person MEANS
    `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` person

§§§ `2(7) governor: the cases (a) to (e) and the answer`

-- The cases (a) to (d): each is a pair of whether the case applies to the entity and whether the person meets it. The residue (e) applies when none of them applies to the entity.
-- Fork F1.4: every case that applies counts (reading A, taken: a director of a company that is the sole trustee is a governor), or only the first (reading B).
@ref Article 2(7)(a) (src:92)
GIVEN kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      person IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
GIVETH A PAIR OF BOOLEAN, BOOLEAN
`Art 2(7)(a) in the case of a trust or fidéicommis, a trustee or fidéicommissaire of the trust or fidéicommis` kinds person MEANS
    PAIR OF (    elem `the trustees of a trust` kinds
             OR  elem `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` kinds)
           , person's `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis`

@ref Article 2(7)(b) (src:93)
GIVEN kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      person IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
GIVETH A PAIR OF BOOLEAN, BOOLEAN
`Art 2(7)(b) in the case of a foundation, a member of the council of the foundation` kinds person MEANS
    PAIR OF elem `a foundation` kinds, person's `a member of the council of the foundation`

@ref Article 2(7)(c) (src:94)
GIVEN kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      person IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
GIVETH A PAIR OF BOOLEAN, BOOLEAN
`Art 2(7)(c) in the case of a company, a director of the company` kinds person MEANS
    PAIR OF elem `a company` kinds, person's `a director of the company`

@ref Article 2(7)(d) (src:95)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      model IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)`
      person IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
GIVETH A PAIR OF BOOLEAN, BOOLEAN
`Art 2(7)(d) in the case of a relevant unincorporated entity, a member of its management committee` interp kinds model person MEANS
    PAIR OF `Art 2(8) the entity is a relevant unincorporated entity` interp kinds model, person's `a member of the management committee of the entity`

@ref Article 2(7) (src:91-96)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      model IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)`
      person IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
GIVETH A LIST OF PAIR OF BOOLEAN, BOOLEAN
`Art 2(7) the cases (a) to (d) for the entity and the person` interp kinds model person MEANS
    LIST `Art 2(7)(a) in the case of a trust or fidéicommis, a trustee or fidéicommissaire of the trust or fidéicommis` kinds person
       , `Art 2(7)(b) in the case of a foundation, a member of the council of the foundation` kinds person
       , `Art 2(7)(c) in the case of a company, a director of the company` kinds person
       , `Art 2(7)(d) in the case of a relevant unincorporated entity, a member of its management committee` interp kinds model person

@ref Article 2(7) (src:91-96)
@export Whether a person is a governor of an entity under Article 2(7) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: a trustee or fidéicommissaire of a trust or fidéicommis, a member of the council of a foundation, a director of a company, a member of the management committee of a relevant unincorporated entity, or in any other case a person who under the constitution has the general control and management of the administration of the entity; for an entity in more than one kind, every case that applies counts (or only the first, on the second reading of fork F1.4); a body that is not an entity has no governor
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork; the field `cases for a body in more than one kind` decides how the cases combine
      kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity` @desc The sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls, as the entity's `kinds of entity`
      model IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` @desc For an unincorporated body: whether its constitution conforms to a model the Commissioner published that provides for a management committee
      person IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity` @desc What the person is to the entity: trustee, council member, director, committee member, and the relation to the general control and management
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` interp kinds model person MEANS
    IF null kinds
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF any fst cases
         THEN any (GIVEN met YIELD met) (`Art 2 the results of the cases that apply` interp cases)
         ELSE `Art 2(7)(e) the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` person
    WHERE
        cases MEANS `Art 2(7) the cases (a) to (d) for the entity and the person` interp kinds model person

-- A person with the facts of the role, as the people of an entity are given.
DECLARE `Person considered as a governor` HAS
    person IS A Governor
        @desc The person, as the shared noun records a governor
    role IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
        @desc What the person is to the entity

@ref Article 2(7) (src:91-96)
@export The people among those given who are governors of an entity under Article 2(7) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, as the list of governors that the shared record of an entity carries
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` @desc The reading taken at each fork
      kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity` @desc The sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls
      model IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` @desc The model constitution facts of Article 2(8)
      people IS A LIST OF `Person considered as a governor` @desc Each person connected with the entity, with the facts of the person's role
GIVETH A LIST OF Governor
`Art 2(7) the governors among the people` interp kinds model people MEANS
    map (GIVEN considered YIELD considered's person)
        (filter (GIVEN considered YIELD `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` interp kinds model (considered's role)) people)

§§§ `2(10) misconduct`

-- src:105 | (10) In this Law, unless the context otherwise requires, “misconduct” means –
-- src:106 | (a) a contravention, by a registered charity or by any of its governors, of a provision –
-- src:107 | (i) of this Law, or of any enactment under this Law,
-- src:108 | (ii) of the constitution of the registered charity, or of the constitutional Law of the charity,
-- src:109 | (iii) of a required steps notice, or
-- src:110 | (iv) of an order of the court under this Law or under the constitutional Law of the charity, or under any enactment under such a Law; or
-- src:111 | (b) the commission by any person, in relation a registered charity or to an excepted foreign charity (within the meaning of Article 22) or to an entity equivalent to a registered charity under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey, of an offence –
-- src:112 | (i) under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity,
-- src:113 | (ii) under the Financial Services (Jersey) Law 1998, the Banking Business (Jersey) Law 1991, the Collective Investment Funds (Jersey) Law 1988, the Insurance Business (Jersey) Law 1996, any Regulation or Order made under any of those Laws, or the Alternative Investment Funds (Jersey) Regulations 2012,
-- src:114 | (iii) under the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961, the Goods and Services Tax (Jersey) Law 2007, or the Taxation (Land Transactions) (Jersey) Law 2009,
-- src:115 | (iv) under any other enactment, being an offence relating to money laundering or terrorist financing,
-- src:116 | (v) under any other enactment or under customary law, being an offence involving deception or dishonesty, or
-- src:117 | (vi) under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey, being an offence similar to any of those listed in clauses (i) to (v).
-- The text of (b) reads "in relation a registered charity": a "to" is missing, in the consolidated text and in the PDF text layer alike; the sense is clear.
-- (vi) says "clauses (i) to (v)"; the Law has no other name for the level of (i) to (v), so this is not shown to be a slip; the sense is clear.
-- What the encoding does not decide, and takes as input: whether a provision of this Law has been contravened (every duty decides its own breach); what the other enactments make an offence;
-- whether an offence is one "involving deception or dishonesty" or one "similar to" those in (i) to (v); and the constitutional Law of a foreign entity.
-- Fork F1.7: "registered charity" is "an entity entered for the time being" in the general or the restricted section. The standing is read at the time of the conduct (reading A, taken: Article 14(1)(a)
-- speaks of "is or has been misconduct", which makes no sense if a deregistration erased the past, and a reading B would let an entity escape the consequences of its misconduct by being deregistered),
-- or when the question is asked (reading B: "for the time being" is present tense, and Article 17(9)(a) needs the counterfactual "would have been misconduct if the entity had not been deregistered",
-- which reads naturally if misconduct is judged by today's standing). The text does not settle it.
-- Fork F1.2: the words "in relation to ..." in (b) govern every limb (i) to (vi) (reading A, taken), or only (i) (reading B).
DECLARE `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)` HAS
    `standing of the entity when the conduct occurred` IS A `Standing on the register`
        @desc Where the entity stood on the register when the conduct occurred
    `standing of the entity when the question is asked` IS A `Standing on the register`
        @desc Where the entity stands on the register on the day the question is asked
    `the constitutional Laws of the charity` IS A LIST OF `Constitutional Law of an entity`
        @desc The constitutional Law of the charity under Article 2(5), as the list Article 2(5) gives; empty where the definition names none
    `an entity equivalent to a registered charity under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(b): the entity is equivalent to a registered charity under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey
    `by the registered charity or by one of its governors` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(a): the conduct is by the registered charity or by one of its governors
    `a contravention of a provision of the constitution of the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(a)(ii): the conduct contravenes a provision of the constitution of the registered charity
    `a contravention of a provision of the constitutional Law of the charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(a)(ii): the conduct contravenes a provision of the constitutional Law of the charity
    `a contravention of a provision of a required steps notice` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(a)(iii): the conduct contravenes a provision of a required steps notice
    `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under this Law` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(a)(iv): the conduct contravenes a provision of an order of the court under this Law
    `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under this Law` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(a)(iv): the conduct contravenes a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under this Law
    `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under the constitutional Law of the charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(a)(iv): the conduct contravenes a provision of an order of the court under the constitutional Law of the charity
    `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under the constitutional Law of the charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(a)(iv): the conduct contravenes a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under the constitutional Law of the charity
    `the offence is in relation to the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(b): the conduct is the commission of an offence in relation to the entity (which is a registered charity, an excepted foreign charity, or an equivalent foreign entity)
    `an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(b)(i)
    `an offence under the financial services Laws, any Regulation or Order made under them, or the Alternative Investment Funds (Jersey) Regulations 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(b)(ii): the Financial Services (Jersey) Law 1998, the Banking Business (Jersey) Law 1991, the Collective Investment Funds (Jersey) Law 1988, the Insurance Business (Jersey) Law 1996, any Regulation or Order under them, or the Alternative Investment Funds (Jersey) Regulations 2012
    `an offence under the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961, the Goods and Services Tax (Jersey) Law 2007 or the Taxation (Land Transactions) (Jersey) Law 2009` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(b)(iii)
    `an offence under any other enactment relating to money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(b)(iv)
    `an offence under any other enactment or under customary law involving deception or dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(b)(v)
    `an offence under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey similar to one listed in (i) to (v)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Article 2(10)(b)(vi): an offence under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey, similar to any of those listed in clauses (i) to (v)

-- The standing of the charity that the conduct is judged against: fork F1.7.
-- src:34 | “registered charity” means an entity entered for the time being in the general section or the restricted section of the register;
@ref Article 1, definition of “registered charity” (src:34)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      conduct IS A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(10) the entity is a registered charity at the time the standing is read` interp conduct MEANS
    `Art 1 the standing is that of a registered charity`
        (CONSIDER interp's `time of the standing of a charity`
         WHEN `when the conduct in Article 2(10) occurred` THEN conduct's `standing of the entity when the conduct occurred`
         WHEN `when the question under Article 2(10) is asked` THEN conduct's `standing of the entity when the question is asked`)

-- (a)(i): of this Law, or of any enactment under this Law. The fact is the standard input IP13.
@ref Article 2(10)(a)(i) (src:107)
GIVEN `the charity or governor has contravened a provision of this Law or an enactment under it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(10)(a)(i) a provision of this Law or of an enactment under it has been contravened` `the charity or governor has contravened a provision of this Law or an enactment under it` MEANS
    `the charity or governor has contravened a provision of this Law or an enactment under it`

-- (a)(ii): of the constitution of the registered charity, or of the constitutional Law of the charity. Where the definition of "constitutional Law" names none, there is no such Law to contravene.
@ref Article 2(10)(a)(ii) (src:108)
GIVEN conduct IS A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(10)(a)(ii) a provision of the constitution or of the constitutional Law of the charity has been contravened` conduct MEANS
        conduct's `a contravention of a provision of the constitution of the registered charity`
    OR  (    NOT null (conduct's `the constitutional Laws of the charity`)
         AND conduct's `a contravention of a provision of the constitutional Law of the charity`)

-- (a)(iii): of a required steps notice. There must be a notice: the notices served on the charity or its governors are the standard input IP19.
@ref Article 2(10)(a)(iii) (src:109)
GIVEN conduct IS A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(10)(a)(iii) a provision of a required steps notice has been contravened` conduct `the required steps notices served` MEANS
        NOT null `the required steps notices served`
    AND conduct's `a contravention of a provision of a required steps notice`

-- (a)(iv): of an order of the court under this Law or under the constitutional Law of the charity, or under any enactment under such a Law.
@ref Article 2(10)(a)(iv) (src:110)
GIVEN conduct IS A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 2(10)(a)(iv) a provision of an order of the court has been contravened` conduct MEANS
        conduct's `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under this Law`
    OR  conduct's `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under this Law`
    OR  (    NOT null (conduct's `the constitutional Laws of the charity`)
         AND (    conduct's `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under the constitutional Law of the charity`
              OR  conduct's `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under the constitutional Law of the charity`))

@ref Article 2(10)(a) (src:106)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      conduct IS A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
      `the charity or governor has contravened a provision of this Law or an enactment under it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
